{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2954","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2954","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2954\",\"parent_revision\":\"88b4b4dd4546ee768e986bef55a0a32245ec1abe\",\"root_revision\":\"18bbd9781401d4e2c46a9e0c908b36b5a267a0c28c691a16c6e1b55b9dcc0d9b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Chore\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-17\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe agentskills.io open Agent Skills spec (verified directly against agentskills.io/specification) does not define bang-exec dynamic context injection or `$ARGUMENTS`/`${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}`/`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` substitution \u2014 body content has \\\"no format restrictions\\\" per spec. These are Claude Code-specific extensions. A spec-only-compliant harness (e.g. Codex, OpenCode) never substitutes them; the model sees literal, unresolved text, and \u2014 per instructions like \\\"Execute the command in `<input/>`\\\" \u2014 may attempt to run that literal text itself via its own shell tool, with unpredictable results (e.g. `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` expanding to empty under real bash, producing a broken absolute path).\\n\\n62 of this repo's SKILL.md files use `$ARGUMENTS`; 23 use bang-exec generally. Only 4 declare the spec's `compatibility` frontmatter field, which exists specifically to disclose exactly this kind of vendor-specific requirement (spec example: `compatibility: Designed for Claude Code (or similar products)`).\\n\\n**User-provided context**: One possible remediation is adding the `compatibility` frontmatter field to every skill using bang-exec, so Codex/OpenCode users get honest signal that the skill requires Claude Code instead of a silent broken execution attempt. This is a suggested direction, not a specified requirement \u2014 scope and approach need review.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the project infrastructure**, I want to **62 skill.md files use claude code-specific dynamic context injection without declaring the open spec's compatibility field** so that **the project infrastructure stays healthy**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 confirmed against the agentskills.io open spec while fixing work-backlog-item's parser\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-17\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1984bea6b01b3379096d51b7b20140713d35e05f1c82c5b2c9796cc3bbd23215\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPUYSCA\"}"}